    <h1>Privacy Policy – Color Pop Jam</h1>
    <p class="date">Effective date: <time datetime="2026-11-06">November 6, 2026</time></p>
    <p>Color Pop Jam (Android package: <span>com.baranatlihan.colorpopjam</span>) is developed and published by Baran Atlıhan, an independent developer responsible for the game's data processing.</p>
    <p>This policy explains how information is processed to operate the game, validate purchases, prevent duplicate grants and fraud, and support privacy choices. Processing depends on the version of the game, enabled features, your region, and your choices. Some testing versions disable purchases, advertising, or optional services.</p>

    <h2>Information We May Process</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Device and app information:</strong> device model, operating system, app version, language, installation identifiers, IP address, and technical request or error information needed by enabled services. Advertising providers may derive an approximate location from network information.</li>
      <li><strong>Guest identifiers:</strong> a Firebase Authentication anonymous user ID and authentication information used to identify a guest securely when communicating with purchase services. An anonymous ID is a technical identifier, not a public profile or a guarantee that data cannot be linked to an installation.</li>
      <li><strong>Purchase information:</strong> product and transaction or order identifiers, purchase tokens or receipts submitted for verification, purchase status, verification results, and records of fulfillment, duplicate checks, and refunds. Records may be associated with a guest ID and installation identifier.</li>
      <li><strong>Local game data:</strong> progress, coin balance, settings, and purchase fulfillment or entitlement state stored on your device. Local game progress is separate from the server's purchase ledger; that ledger is not a cloud backup of your game.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising information, when ads are enabled:</strong> advertising identifiers where permitted, ad requests, impressions, interactions, and consent choices.</li>
      <li><strong>Support information:</strong> your email address and any details you choose to send when contacting the developer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Anonymous Guest Account and Recovery Limits</h2>
    <p>The game uses Firebase Authentication in Anonymous Guest mode for features such as authenticated purchase verification. You do not enter an email address or password to create this guest identity. <strong>The initial release does not offer Google sign-in, email sign-in, or account linking.</strong></p>
    <p><strong>If you uninstall the game, clear its app data, or change devices, restoration of your progress and purchased coin balance is not guaranteed.</strong> These actions can remove local data or leave you with a new anonymous account. A Google Play purchase history does not by itself provide a backup of spent or remaining coins or gameplay progress.</p>
    <p><strong>Remove Ads is a permanent, non-consumable store product, but automatic transfer of ownership to a new anonymous account is not guaranteed.</strong> Any ownership check depends on available store evidence and the game's verification process. There is no guaranteed cross-device or reinstall recovery service in the initial release.</p>
    <p>These technical recovery limitations do not limit your applicable consumer, refund, or data protection rights. Contact support for purchase problems; support cannot promise restoration that the available records do not support.</p>

    <h2>Google Play Purchases and Verification</h2>
    <p>Google Play handles payments for coin packs of 250, 750, and 2,000 coins and for Remove Ads, when purchases are enabled. Payment card details are handled by Google Play and its payment providers; the game does not directly collect your payment card details.</p>
    <p>Purchase information is sent to Firebase Cloud Functions for server-side verification with Google Play. Cloud Firestore stores a transaction ledger to track verification and fulfillment, prevent duplicate grants, and handle refunded or revoked transactions. The service associates relevant records with the guest and installation involved in the purchase. Purchase verification and fraud prevention are separate from optional gameplay analytics.</p>

    <h2>Advertising and Consent</h2>
    <p>The game's advertising integrations include Google AdMob and Unity LevelPlay. When advertising is enabled, these services and the advertising partners serving an ad may process device and network information, advertising identifiers where permitted, and ad interaction information to deliver and measure ads and prevent abuse.</p>
    <p>Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) manages applicable advertising consent messages and privacy options. Advertising that requires consent depends on the applicable consent state. The availability of personalized, limited, or other advertising depends on the region, enabled providers, and privacy choices; declining personalization does not necessarily remove all ads or all technical processing.</p>
    <p>Where available or required, use the game's Privacy Options control to review or change advertising consent. You can also manage advertising ID and ad privacy settings on your Android device. Buying Remove Ads is an advertising entitlement, not a request to delete data or change consent.</p>

    <h2>Analytics, Attribution, and Diagnostics</h2>
    <p><strong>Optional telemetry is disabled in the current release configuration.</strong> GameAnalytics, AppsFlyer, Firebase Analytics, and Firebase Crashlytics have integration support in the project, but are not active optional data collection services in this configuration. Their presence in the project does not mean they receive gameplay events, attribution events, or crash reports.</p>
    <p>If a later release enables optional analytics, attribution, or crash reporting, this policy will be updated to describe the enabled providers, purposes, and relevant data, such as gameplay events, device or installation identifiers, and crash diagnostics. Any collection requiring consent must follow the applicable privacy choices.</p>
    <p>Enabled online services may still process technical request, error, and security logs to operate authentication, purchase verification, advertising, or support. This operational processing is distinct from optional analytics. Firebase Remote Config may retrieve game settings and process the installation and request information needed for that service; it does not provide account linking or a backup of progress.</p>

    <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>Local progress and settings remain on your device until removed by game or device actions. Uninstalling the game or clearing app data can remove local records, but does not automatically delete server-side purchase records or information already held by Google Play or other service providers.</p>
    <p>Guest and transaction records are retained as needed to operate purchase verification, prevent duplicate fulfillment and fraud, handle refunds or disputes, and meet applicable legal obligations. Retention depends on the record and its purpose; this policy does not promise an automatic deletion deadline or permanent storage. Service providers also apply their own retention practices.</p>
    <p>To request access to or deletion of data associated with your guest identity, email <a href="mailto:baranatlihan9@gmail.com">baranatlihan9@gmail.com</a> and name Color Pop Jam. We may ask for the minimum information needed to locate the records and verify your request. If you have already lost access to your guest identity, identifying the relevant records may be difficult. Do not send passwords, authentication tokens, full purchase tokens, or payment card details.</p>
    <p>Requests are handled subject to applicable law. Some transaction or security records may need to be retained for legal obligations, fraud prevention, or resolving disputes; we will explain any applicable limits. You may also need to manage information held independently by Google Play or another provider through that provider's privacy controls.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
    <p>Information is processed by providers needed for enabled features, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google and Google Play</a>: payment processing, store purchase records, and advertising or consent services such as AdMob and UMP.</li>
      <li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Google Firebase and Google Cloud</a>: anonymous authentication, Cloud Functions purchase verification, Firestore transaction records, Remote Config, and related operational processing.</li>
      <li><a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy">Unity LevelPlay and participating advertising providers</a>: ad mediation and delivery when advertising is enabled.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The optional analytics, attribution, and crash reporting integrations described above are not presented as active providers in the current configuration. Providers process information under their applicable terms and privacy policies and may process it outside your country. Information may also be disclosed when required by law or necessary to address fraud, security incidents, or legal claims.</p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Color Pop Jam is intended for a general audience and is not specifically directed to children. We do not knowingly seek personal contact information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate steps. Applicable age, regional, and store requirements govern advertising and consent; a general-audience designation does not authorize unrestricted collection from children.</p>

    <h2>Your Privacy Choices and Rights</h2>
    <p>You can review available in-game consent options, change Android advertising privacy settings, manage purchases through Google Play, and contact us about your data. Withdrawing consent affects future processing based on that consent; it does not automatically remove information lawfully processed earlier. Essential purchase and security processing does not depend on opting into optional analytics.</p>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or obtain a copy of your personal data, restrict or object to certain processing, withdraw consent, or complain to your local data protection authority. Contact the developer to exercise applicable rights. You do not need to waive these rights to use support or request help with a purchase.</p>

    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the game, enabled services, or applicable requirements change. The current version and effective date are available on this page.</p>

    <h2>Contact and Support</h2>
    <p>Developer: Baran Atlıhan<br>Game: Color Pop Jam<br>Privacy questions, deletion requests, and purchase support: <a href="mailto:baranatlihan9@gmail.com">baranatlihan9@gmail.com</a></p>
